.TH RETA\-MOJO\-PARALLEL\-EXECUTION 1 "July 2026" "reta_arch_mojo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
reta\-mojo\-parallel\-execution \- native parallel execution checker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reta\-mojo\-parallel\-execution
.RI [ ARGUMENT ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B reta\-mojo\-parallel\-execution
runs the native Mojo parallel execution tool. It is mainly a diagnostic, parity, architecture, or release\-check command for the ongoing port rather than a normal end\-user frontend.

.SH NOTES
This command is installed because it is a build or diagnostic target of the native Mojo port. Normal users usually start with .BR reta (1), .BR rp (1), .BR rpl (1), .BR rpe (1), or .BR rpb (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success and non-zero on errors, failed checks, missing build targets, or invalid arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR reta(1), rp(1), rpl(1), rpe(1), rpb(1), reta-mojo(1)
